config ROBA_FORCE_BT_NAME
    bool "Overwrite the stored Bluetooth name with CONFIG_BT_DEVICE_NAME at boot"
    default y if ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && BT_DEVICE_NAME_DYNAMIC && BT_SETTINGS
    help
      Zephyr restores a previously stored Bluetooth name (setting bt/name) and
      prefers it over the firmware default, so a renamed firmware keeps the old
      name. This re-applies CONFIG_BT_DEVICE_NAME a few seconds after boot.
      Enabled only on the central (right) half. See src/force_bt_name.c.
